---
title: Loading & Reloading
description: Choose between direct loading, retained loaders, and the fluent builder.
---

## Direct objects and retained loaders

`Yacla.yaml<T>()` and `Yacla.json<T>()` return `T`. Their `autoUpdate` argument defaults to `false` and their logger defaults to null.

Keep a `ConfigLoader<T>` when your application needs to reload:

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.Yacla
import net.ririfa.yacla.yaml.yamlLoader
import java.nio.file.Paths

val loader = Yacla.yamlLoader<AppConfig>(
    resource = "/defaults/config.yml",
    file = Paths.get("config.yml"),
    autoUpdate = true
)

val initialConfig = loader.config
loader.reload()
val refreshedConfig = loader.config
```

`reload()` reads the backing file and replaces the loader's current config snapshot. Previously retrieved objects still refer to the old snapshot. Reloading does not itself perform an update check.

## Builder

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.Yacla
import net.ririfa.yacla.yaml.YamlParser
import java.nio.file.Paths

val loader = Yacla.loader<AppConfig>()
    .fromResource("/defaults/config.yml")
    .toFile(Paths.get("config.yml"))
    .parser(YamlParser())
    .autoUpdateIfOutdated(true)
    .load()
```

For ordinary loading, set a resource, a target file, and a parser before `load()`. Use `pull(...)` instead of `toFile(...)` for [localized defaults](/yacla/localization/).

The format-specific DSL preselects its parser:

```kotlin
val loader = Yacla.yamlLoader<AppConfig> {
    fromResource("/defaults/config.yml")
    toFile(Paths.get("config.yml"))
    autoUpdateIfOutdated(true)
}
```

## Lifecycle reference

| Member | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `config` | Returns the current in-memory config |
| `reload()` | Parses and validates the file again; returns the loader |
| `updateConfig()` | Checks and merges the resource; returns whether the file changed |

After a successful manual update, call `reload()` to read the updated file. There is no automatic file watcher.

## Constructor defaults without I/O

```kotlin
val defaults = Yacla.fillByDefault<AppConfig>()
```

This directly invokes the Kotlin primary constructor with no arguments. Every constructor parameter must have a default value. It performs no file access, parsing, or annotation validation.
